---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { newest, entries } from '../data/entries';
const latest = newest[0];
const selected = entries.filter(e => e.milestone).slice(0, 3);
---
<Base title="Home">
  <section class="hero"><div><p class="eyebrow">My game project / notes from along the way</p><h1>They Forgot the Alamo</h1><p class="lead">A man wakes up thinking he's Davy Crockett. He's got a shotgun, a room he can tear apart, and—where his hat ought to be—a raccoon. That's the game I'm trying to make.</p><p>Right now: a playable room prototype. Latest update: October 2, 2026.</p><div class="actions"><a class="button" href="/play/">How to play</a><a class="button secondary" href="/devlog/">My project notes</a><a class="button secondary" href="/timeline/">See how it grew</a></div></div><div class="hero-media"><img src="/media/two-hand-carry.webp" alt="October 2 game capture of Davy holding the shotgun" fetchpriority="high" /></div></section>
  <section class="section"><div class="section-head"><div><p class="eyebrow">What changed most recently</p><h2>Latest update</h2></div><a href="/devlog/">All my notes →</a></div><div class="split"><img src={latest.image || '/media/current-room.webp'} alt={latest.imageAlt || latest.title} loading="lazy" /><div><p class="date">{latest.date} / I was working on…</p><h3><a href={'/devlog/'+latest.slug+'/'}>{latest.title}</a></h3><p>{latest.summary}</p><a class="button secondary" href={'/devlog/'+latest.slug+'/'}>Read the note</a></div></div></section>
  <section class="section"><div class="section-head"><div><p class="eyebrow">A few big steps</p><h2>How it got here</h2></div><a href="/timeline/">See the whole timeline →</a></div><div class="grid">{selected.map(e => <a class="card milestone" href={'/devlog/'+e.slug+'/'}>{e.image && <img src={e.image} alt={e.imageAlt} loading="lazy" />}<div class="card-content"><span class="date">{e.date}</span><h3>{e.title}</h3><p>{e.summary}</p></div></a>)}</div></section>
  <section class="section"><p class="eyebrow">Then / now</p><h2>From boxes to Davy</h2><p>The earliest saved build uses simple shapes for Davy. Later versions add a character model, animation, and a shotgun grip that has had a frankly unreasonable number of reviews.</p><div class="comparison"><figure><img src="/media/first-commit-room.webp" alt="First surviving game build from September 29, reconstructed in a browser" loading="lazy" /><figcaption>Then / saved September 29 build, reconstructed October 1</figcaption></figure><figure><img src="/media/two-hand-carry.webp" alt="October 2 game room capture with Davy carrying the shotgun" loading="lazy" /><figcaption>Now / October 2 review capture</figcaption></figure></div></section>
  <section class="section"><p class="eyebrow">Where the build is at</p><h2>What exists so far</h2><div class="grid"><div><h3>Things you can do</h3><p>Move around, aim, fire the two-shell shotgun, reload it, break targets and bits of wall, and take a little raccoon detour with Q.</p></div><div><h3>Still open</h3><p>Davy's movement and look, the graphics, and how this one test room becomes an actual game.</p></div><div><h3>The notes</h3><p>{entries.length} notes about the builds I can still check, including {entries.filter(e=>e.milestone).length} bigger milestones. The oldest verifiable game version is September 29.</p></div></div></section>
</Base>
